# The cache root every M1 run is pointed at (`tools/run-member.ts`). Derived data, never committed.
#
# Two reasons it exists at all, given that every M1 run passes `--no-cache`. First, `run.ts` needs a
# cache root even with the cache off — it just writes under `<root>/disabled/<pid>` — and the root it
# would otherwise use is the *home worktree's* `data/devloop-cache/` when running a member's original,
# which would be a write into a worktree P4 must only read. Second, the same redirection keeps p4's
# own runs out of `research/v3/data/devloop/`, which P4 does not own either.
#
# Self-ignoring, following `research/v3/data/devloop-cache/.gitignore`'s own note on why the rule
# lives in the directory rather than in a shared `.gitignore` another workstream may have in flight.
*
!.gitignore
